# CoreSuite

Windows-first suite of Tauri 2 programs: `editor`, `explorer`, `terminal`.

## Placement

- Shared Rust → `crates/{core,shell,cli}`
- Shared TS/Svelte → `packages/{shell-ui,shell-bridge,tsconfig}`
- App-only → `programs/<name>/`
- Never copy a feature into all three programs. Extract, then import.
- Scaffold files are empty. Establish a pattern in the shared layer first, then use it in one program.

## Tooling

pnpm workspaces, Turbo, Cargo workspace, Vitest, Playwright, NSIS. Details: `.cursor/context/` (read the matching pack). Versions: `.cursor/context/versions.md` + `.cursor/cache/`.

## Security

Capabilities JSON is the security boundary. Do not widen allowlists to "make it work".

## Agent

- Shell is PowerShell. Prefer `node` scripts over bash.
- Use already-available Context7 for Tauri/Rust/Svelte docs. Do not add project MCP servers.
- Do not "complete" the empty repo unless asked. Change only what the task needs.
